---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Choosing Pi and the first Durable configuration
  accDescr: Choose Pi Coding Agent for a person working in a local terminal, or Pi Durable 1.3.0 when building an application that owns restart recovery and client state. For Durable, start with SQLite, direct tools, and foreground owned work. Choose Memory for disposable tests, JSONL for readable small logs, code mode for multi-call composition, and background work only when its lifetime must survive parent abort.

  Need["What are you building?"]:::csPrimary
  Terminal["A person working<br/>in a local terminal"]:::csMuted
  Coding["Pi Coding Agent<br/>Interactive / print / JSON / RPC"]:::csPrimary
  subgraph Application[" "]
    App["An application with restart recovery<br/>or multiple clients"]:::csMuted
    Durable["Pi Durable 1.3.0<br/>Host owns storage, models, registry, env"]:::csPrimary
    Storage["Storage"]:::csAccent
    StoreDefault["SQLite: default<br/>Memory: disposable tests<br/>JSONL: readable small logs"]:::csMuted
    Tools["Tool composition"]:::csAccent
    ToolDefault["Direct tools: default<br/>Code mode: multiple calls in JavaScript"]:::csMuted
    Lifetime["Work lifetime"]:::csAccent
    LifeDefault["Foreground owned work: default<br/>Background: survive parent abort"]:::csMuted
    App --> Durable
    Durable --> Storage --> StoreDefault
    Durable --> Tools --> ToolDefault
    Durable --> Lifetime --> LifeDefault
  end
  style Application fill:#ffffff,stroke:none

  Need --> Terminal --> Coding
  Need --> App
  classDef csPrimary fill:#9e1b32,stroke:none,color:#ffffff,stroke-width:0px;
  classDef csAccent fill:#000000,stroke:none,color:#ffffff,stroke-width:0px;
  classDef csMuted fill:#828282,stroke:none,color:#000000,stroke-width:0px;
